𝗙𝗜𝗥𝗦𝗧 𝗕𝗔𝗧𝗖𝗛 | 𝗣𝗢𝗪𝗘𝗥 𝗕𝗜 𝗠𝗜𝗡𝗜 𝗣𝗥𝗢𝗝𝗘𝗖𝗧 𝗥𝗘𝗙𝗘𝗥𝗘𝗡𝗖𝗘 #𝟬𝟮


𝗡𝗘𝗧𝗙𝗟𝗜𝗫 𝗔𝗡𝗔𝗟𝗬𝗧𝗜𝗖𝗦 𝗗𝗔𝗦𝗛𝗕𝗢𝗔𝗥𝗗


As part of the First Batch Power BI Master Class & Internship, I created trainer-led reference dashboards to demonstrate how a Power BI mini project can be structured, analyzed, and presented through an interactive dashboard.


𝗧𝗵𝗶𝘀 𝗡𝗲𝘁𝗳𝗹𝗶𝘅 𝗔𝗻𝗮𝗹𝘆𝘁𝗶𝗰𝘀 𝗗𝗮𝘀𝗵𝗯𝗼𝗮𝗿𝗱 𝗶𝘀 𝗥𝗲𝗳𝗲𝗿𝗲𝗻𝗰𝗲 #𝟬𝟮 𝗶𝗻 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝘀𝗲𝗿𝗶𝗲𝘀.


𝗞𝗲𝘆 𝗮𝗻𝗮𝗹𝘆𝘁𝗶𝗰𝗮𝗹 𝗮𝗿𝗲𝗮𝘀 𝗶𝗻𝗰𝗹𝘂𝗱𝗲:


• Total Movie Count — 1K  
• Average Rating — 8  
• Release Count — 672  
• Movie Count by Genre  
• Movie Release Trend by Year  
• Movie Rating Categories  
• Average Rating by Genre  
• Detailed Movie-Level Data  
• Genre-based Interactive Filtering


𝗚𝗲𝗻𝗿𝗲 𝗮𝗻𝗮𝗹𝘆𝘀𝗶𝘀 𝗵𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝘀:


• Action — 263 movies  
• Drama — 247 movies  
• Comedy — 239 movies


The dashboard also presents a year-wise movie trend, rating category distribution, and average rating comparison across Action, Comedy, and Drama genres.


𝗣𝗼𝘄𝗲𝗿 𝗕𝗜 𝗙𝗢𝗖𝗨𝗦:


Data → Analysis → Visualization → Interactive Reporting


The purpose of this reference dashboard was to demonstrate how multiple KPIs, charts, tables, slicers, and analytical views can be brought together into a single Power BI report.


𝗧𝗵𝗶𝘀 𝗶𝘀 𝗮 𝗧𝗥𝗔𝗜𝗡𝗘𝗥-𝗖𝗥𝗘𝗔𝗧𝗘𝗗 𝗥𝗘𝗙𝗘𝗥𝗘𝗡𝗖𝗘 𝗗𝗔𝗦𝗛𝗕𝗢𝗔𝗥𝗗 — 𝗻𝗼𝘁 𝗮 𝗽𝗮𝗿𝘁𝗶𝗰𝗶𝗽𝗮𝗻𝘁 𝘀𝘂𝗯𝗺𝗶𝘀𝘀𝗶𝗼𝗻.


It was created to help First Batch participants understand how to approach a domain-based Power BI mini project and develop their own analytical dashboards.


